   "notes": "Organism is Bacillus subtilis (BSF1 and genome-reduced derivatives); cultivation was strictly aerobic shake-flask (37 C, 220-240 rpm, 100 mL in 500 mL flasks), so oxygen is aerobic rather than facultative. Main text gives only the three supplements over M9; the base M9 salts + FeCl3 + full trace-element mix were recovered from the cited Harwood & Cutting 1990 B. subtilis M9 (SubtiWiki formulation, same reference). This M9 contains no vitamins (no thiamine). The only trace element truly absent from the prior component set was molybdenum (Mo); Fe, Mn, Zn, Cu, Co were already present as open exch"
